The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ret = vgic_its_resolve_lpi(kvm, its, irq_entry->msi.devid, irq_entry->msi.data, &irq);
if (ret)
    goto out;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because there is no check to see if the virtual Low Priority Interrupt (vLPI) has already been mapped after resolving the LPI. If the `irq->hw` flag is not checked before attempting to map the vLPI, it can lead to multiple mapping attempts on the same vLPI, causing errors or undefined behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (irq->hw)
    goto out;
```
Reason:
This added check ensures that if the `irq->hw` flag is already set (indicating that the vLPI is already mapped), the function will exit early without attempting to perform another mapping. This prevents the issue of multiple mappings for the same vLPI, thus maintaining the integrity of the KVM's interrupt handling logic.

